|passage=A code '''one-eight-seven''' on Jefferson one-four-eight-nine. Corner store—7-Eleven." A '''187''' was a homicide, Jefferson, the other side of town. ...}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2003|author=Mark Anthony Neal|title=Songs in the Key of Black Life: A Rhythm and Blues Nation|page=164
|passage=[…] and Snoop Dogg blatantly rapped about doing "'''187''' on an undercover cop" on [….]}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Malcolm W. Klein|title=Gang Cop: The Words and Ways of Officer Paco Domingo|page=131
|passage=Paco came across a wall that, in the large block letters of local Hispanic gang graffiti, spelled out “'''187''' Domingo.” This was the ultimate threat for Paco [….]}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Stephen J. Cannell|title=Vertical Coffin|page=256
|passage=Perp at this address is a possible '''One-eight-seven''' P. Request a unit respond Code Three." The RTO came back immediately and put out the call division-wide.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Cash Pawley|title=Pray for Death|page=21
|passage=Respond to a '''one-eight-seven''' at nine-eight-six Cove Road North," the dispatcher continued in her heavy southern drawl. "10-4... En route.[….]}}

